 {:id "d86c8544-2168-48de-a205-dd1f378268ee", :title "Bug: village-feed cases (feeds-three-bread, feeds-two-bread-taken-within-4s, str", :column "live", :commits ["779ff9aa5","bdefaddd"],
 :description "World sweep 461b0141 (body ProbeSweepG), all three failed twice (new fixture village-feed): feeds-three-bread: no event feed.done within 90 s; feeds-two-bread-taken-within-4s and stray-bread-stays: no feed.done {:fed 2} within 40 s. Logs: /home/dan/programs/python/minecraft-agents/.claude/world-sweep-461b0141/world-1791379038521-GmC3tjY-2.log (first), world-1791386210663-x8SYY3c-2.log (rerun).",
 :plan-notes ["Cause (about 70%): the fixture's villager is NoAI, which does not collect dropped items. Log evidence: case 2 gave up not-taken at 16 s (3 tosses x 4 s watch), bread 8 afterwards (all collected back), the stray bread stayed. Job, toss primitive and takenBy receipt unchanged since the 4 s window; no commit since 461b0141 touches feed. No red run is possible (live-only). Fix bdefaddd: fixture summons villagers with movement_speed 0 (AI on, stays put). Live plan: run village-feed.edn all 5 cases. Should succeed: feeds-three-bread (feed.done, bread 5), feeds-two-bread-taken-within-4s (fed 2, no item entities), stray-bread-stays (fed 2, stray bread still there). Should fail: absent-villager-is-gone (gone), full-villager-takes-nothing (not-taken). If it still fails: the toss lands outside pickup reach from 2 blocks; then check the drop position vs the villager, and the playerCollect receipt for a villager collector."]}
 {:id "afdc32d0-3fa3-4997-b4de-4b7c65719182", :title "Trial Sorrel #12: body stuck, every walk \"no path (start-not-standable)\" while i", :column "live", :commits ["1229fa27f","5ae0ad306"],
 :description "Trial 2026-10-14 on job-contract. Sorrel #12 (/home/dan/ws/Sorrel/notes/bugs.md):\n- After j3026 ended at [200.5 75 -125.3], every job that walks fails. `jobs.gather.mine {... :here true}` says \"gave up walking to [200 75 -125]: no path (start-not-standable)\" and tunnels 0 blocks.\n- `jobs.access.stair {:y 16 :here true}` fails the same way, then reports \"undercuts-way at [200 74 -125]: the cell is the floor of a stair this body cut earlier\".\n- A snapshot shows the body on plain dirt at 200 74 -125.\n- Expected: the cell it stands on counts as standable. A stuck start should be escaped (go-to / unwedge), not reported on every job.\n- Find the cause in the start-cell check (the z fraction -125.3 is near an edge? A stair ledger entry that marks the cell?). Test-first.",
 :plan-notes ["Committed and landed on job-contract: 5ae0ad306. Unit: red 2 of 8, then green 229 (planner-start-edge, executor, stairs/courses/slime/swim physics, planner-test); golden 35 passed. Live plan, should succeed: (1) stand a probe 0.69 into a cell whose floor is air, with the neighbour at +z holding a floor (dig the block under [x y-1 z] while the body sneaks to the edge, pos z frac about .69, y unchanged), then go-to 5 blocks away: it plans, steps back onto the neighbour cell first, then arrives. (2) Repeat the Sorrel case: a night dig-in beside an old stair hole, then mine :here; it walks. Should fail: (3) a body truly over a hole (box overlapping no floored cell) still gets start-not-standable and never plans from a cell it does not touch. The stair \"undercuts-way\" refusal is the stair's own ledger rule and is unchanged."]}
 {:id "b812e8f8-092e-4279-844f-35cc90f53a3e", :title "Design D57: farm.till handles coarse dirt and rooted dirt (two hoe uses)", :column "live", :commits ["1229fa27f","6c3f1a24e"],
 :description "Wave now (bug fix, not blocked by Z1). Source: design-summary.md D57.\nWhat: farm.till treats coarse dirt and rooted dirt as tillable: first hoe use turns it to dirt, second to farmland.\nFiles: farm.till (jobs/farm), its tests.\nRisk: low.\nTest plan: unit (coarse -> dirt -> farmland cell sequence, rooted dirt); live fixture: till a plot containing coarse dirt; no soak.",
 :plan-notes ["Committed and landed on job-contract 6c3f1a24e. till-test red 1 of 36, then green; 139 over till, find-spot, farm-contract, farm-tend-plan, sensing-farm, seen-work-reads. Tillable now includes coarse/rooted dirt; the first use (before coarse/rooted, after dirt) counts no try. Unit test uses a useOn override (fake not changed). Live plan: fixture tilling a plot with coarse_dirt and rooted_dirt cells; should succeed: all farmland, 2 hoe uses per such cell; should fail: stone cell in the box is skipped :not-tillable."]}
 {:id "1436e972-44d4-4db3-bdea-38c8064b4272", :title "Trial Sorrel #5: get-kit ends :no-food though the body's own pit of 5 cows + 3 s", :column "live", :commits ["1229fa27f","c7fc56656"],
 :description "Trial 2026-10-14, Sorrel #5. j2963 (get-kit) ended `:cause :no-food :min-food 20 :why \"no food: carried none, searched for animals and ripe crops within 48 blocks, explored: started; no food source is known\"`. The body was near [221 96 -74]. Its own pit at 184..188 x -101..-93 held 5+ cows and 3 sheep, and a wheat field was nearby.\n- **Expected:** the body's own penned animals and its own crops count as food sources. Owner Q189 (penned animals are off limits) is about other players' pens: check which rule excluded them, and whether \"own\" is known from plans or claims.\n- **Also:** :min-food 20 is a high bar at food 14.\n- **Find:** why the search found none; whether it was the pen exclusion, sight, or unripe wheat.\n- **Test-first.**",
 :plan-notes ["fixer-trial-lowhp: landed c7fc56656 on job-contract. get-food has a new last way :pen (after the wild food in reach, before fishing and the search). It hunts the surplus of the body's own zones and plans: keep-adults 2, rule :own-pen. With none in sight, it walks to the nearest own zone or plan within :source-radius 64 not visited in this job. Other enclosures and others' zones stay spared. Tests: own pen only → kills 1 of 3 (:own-pen); wild first; walks to an out-of-sight own pen (red before, green now). Not done: wheat is still never harvested, and Sorrel's wheat fields are in no zone or plan, so own crops count only as non-wheat crops in sight (follow-up card below). :min-food 20 for get-kit unchanged. Live plan: Sorrel at [221 96 -74] by day, hungry, no food; the sunken-pen zone (owner Sorrel) holds 5+ cows → get-food walks to ~[186 111 -95] and kills one cow, keeping 2 adults per kind (should-succeed). Should-fail: a body whose only pen is in another's zone ends :no-food with \"pen\"/\"refused\" passed over."]}
